                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in F
                is bounded below and above by rational numbers, and thus strictly not an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite"} infinite
                element. This also implies that there are no infinitesimal elements, because there are no element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in F
                whose multiplicative inverse is an infinite element.
            %li
