          %h2#category_of_archimedean_ordered_fields Category of Archimedean ordered fields
          %p
            The
            %strong category of Archimedean ordered fields
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are Archimedean ordered fields and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphisms"} ring homomorphisms
            between Archimedean ordered fields. (Every ring homomorphism between Archimedean ordered field can be proven to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strictly+monotonic"} strictly monotonic
            field
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
          %p
            The category of Archimedean ordered fields is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+category"} thin category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+category"} skeletal category
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gaunt+category"} gaunt category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            which consists of all the Archimedean ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfields"} subfields
            of the real numbers.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            in the category of Archimedean ordered fields is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in the category of Archimedean ordered fields is the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+number"}> Dedekind
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %p
            More generally, one can consider, for every sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            \-frame
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \subseteq \Omega
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+truth+values"} frame of truth values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and ring homomorphisms between Archimedean ordered fields admissible for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            in this category, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in this object is a version
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cuts"} Dedekind cuts
            valued in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_\Sigma \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}_D
            is not provably an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p Archimedean ordered fields include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
              (terminal Archimedean ordered field where every element merely has a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locator"} locator
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book+real+numbers"} HoTT book real numbers
              (initial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+complete"} Cauchy complete
              Archimedean ordered field)
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
              (terminal Archimedean ordered field, also initial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+complete"} Dedekind complete
              Archimedean ordered field)
          %p
            These notions of real numbers are the same if every Dedekind real number merely has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locator"} locator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
            imply that every Dedekind real number has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locator"} locator
          %p Non-Archimedean ordered fields include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surreal+numbers"} surreal numbers
